  "details": "Alright here is the issue, I’m on 1313 but playing a world we updated 1306 to 1311. It won’t let me join any worlds we made during this time with 1313 but it wants me to update to 1314 but it’s not network compatible. I can’t join nor create an instance on any world we have made between version 1306-1311, 1311 being the most broken worlds. Telling me to update our client when we have double checked we are on the right one. Any world we have made before these versions works fine and others have also had this issue too. \n\nI’ve attached 2 photos, of the version and the error message and I get this for both creating an instance and joining a world that is “on the correct client”\n\n(Yes I’ve restarted, reinstalled and all the other general procedures, non mitigate this) (Confirmed on quest by a couple of people who can’t even join their home world even though the world client and theirs is up to date) needs confirmation on pc\n\nTry inviting yourself to an instance too that is one way we got this issue.\n\n————————————————\n\n(I was the creator of both instances inviting myself off the website, then joining a public)\n\nI am on 1313\n\n—————\n\nSmall edit, I even tried inviting to our private world I just updated via 1313 just now and it still gave the same error",
